# Problem

Declaring a nixosSystem or darwinSystem requires knowledge of x86_64 vs aarch64.

This knowledge is reliant on the declaration of nixpkgs.hostPlatform in /profiles/{profile}/configuration.nix, which is reliant on the system build to evaluate.

The declaration ({nixos|darwin}System), is also reliant on the host and nixos/darwin, in order to know which modules are needed (a host pulls in a hardware profile, and a system role).

## Current plan

I am thinking of transitioning towards the default.nix or registry.nix.

This get's a bit finicky on darwin/linux separation (darwin-registry.nix and linux-registry.nix may need to be explicitely created and pulled into default|registry.nix)

